task_id: sql_0023
task_type: sql
instruction: "The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. For each bill of materials show the company and lists of all the products and materials. The result must contain exactly one row per bill and be sorted by the company. Write one row per line as bill_id;company;products;materials. Each list is a string of values separated with comma (no spaces) with the values sorted alphabetically; an empty list is an empty string. Sort rows by company name first, then by bill_id. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt)."
reward: 5
